<title>JAPAN: TABLE-JAPAN JAN-JUNE C/A SURPLUS UP 40.4 PCT YR/YR.</title>
<headline>TABLE-JAPAN JAN-JUNE C/A SURPLUS UP 40.4 PCT YR/YR.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The surplus in Japan's current account, the broadest measure of trade in goods and services, rose 40.4 percent to 5.05 trillion yen in the January to June period from a year earlier, the Finance Ministry announced on Friday.</p>
<p>The surplus in merchandise trade alone rose 19.6 percent from the same period a year earlier to 5.18 trillion yen.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the balance of payments figures: (Unadjusted, in bln yen) JAN-JUNE    YEAR AGO</p>
<p>Current Acct Balance     +5,054.1     +3,599.4</p>
<p> -Goods and Services     +1,982.3     +1,121.4</p>
<p>    Trade Balance	  +5,182.0     +4,332.8</p>
<p>	 Exports	     24,088.1     20,941.9</p>
<p>	 Imports	     18,906.1     16,609.1</p>
<p>    Services Balance     -3,199.7	-3211.4</p>
<p> -Income Balance	   +3,693.2     +3,000.0</p>
<p> -Current Transfers	  -621.4	 -522.0</p>
<p>The following figures show the unadjusted balance in Japan's capital and financial accounts (in billion yen):</p>
<p>				JAN-JUNE    YEAR AGO</p>
<p>Capital/Financial Acct -6,364.2	+267.0</p>
<p> -Financial Account    -6,157.4	+499.2</p>
<p>  Direct Investment    -1,441.0    -1,374.8</p>
<p>  Portfolio Investment -4,516.7    +1,016.6</p>
<p>  Other Investment	 -199.7	+857.3</p>
<p> -Capital Account	  -206.8	-232.2</p>
<p>The following figures show the adjusted balance of payments figures (in billions of yen)</p>
<p>				   JAN-JUNE	YEAR AGO</p>
<p>Current Account Balance     +5,126.4	+3,655.1</p>
<p> -Goods and Services	  +2,269.7	+1,060.5</p>
<p>    Trade Balance	     +5,494.7	+4,556.6</p>
<p>	 Exports		  24,643.6	22,201.8</p>
<p>	 Imports		  19,148.9	17,645.2</p>
<p>    Services Balance	  -3,225.0	-3,496.2</p>
<p> -Income Balance		+3,491.8	+3,026.9</p>
<p> -Current Transfers	     -635.2	  -432.2</p>
</text>
